WEBVTT

00:36.161 --> 00:38.955
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

00:42.584 --> 00:44.919
Why did you want to make a film
about the weather?

00:46.171 --> 00:47.088
I don't know.

00:47.797 --> 00:49.007
I have a feeling,

00:49.716 --> 00:50.884
but I can't explain it.

00:51.801 --> 00:52.969
I like that phrase.

00:53.636 --> 00:54.971
"I can't explain it."

00:57.056 --> 00:59.559
You're the first person I've met
who said they like the phrase,

01:00.101 --> 01:01.436
"I can't explain it."

01:03.146 --> 01:06.775
For over-explainers
who have to put everything into words,

01:06.858 --> 01:09.194
hearing that something can't be explained
is probably scary.

01:09.819 --> 01:10.695
But I find myself

01:11.196 --> 01:13.782
waking up when I hear someone admit

01:13.865 --> 01:15.575
they can't explain something.

01:15.658 --> 01:18.078
"Of course, you can't explain it."

01:19.370 --> 01:23.041
"How do you translate abstract thoughts
into concrete words?"

01:26.753 --> 01:27.837
So that's what it was.

01:28.713 --> 01:30.548
The gap between abstract thoughts

01:30.632 --> 01:32.467
and concrete words.

01:33.218 --> 01:34.219
Those two

01:34.844 --> 01:38.181
will never meet,
even if they circle the Earth 20 times.

01:38.973 --> 01:40.558
Even so,

01:40.642 --> 01:42.310
may I try to explain

01:42.393 --> 01:44.771
why I wanted to make a movie
about the weather?

01:45.939 --> 01:48.024
I find myself
wanting to explain it to someone

01:49.484 --> 01:51.069
who knows the limits of language.

01:52.195 --> 01:53.029
Okay.

01:53.822 --> 01:54.656
It's just

01:55.824 --> 01:56.950
a feeling.

02:00.245 --> 02:01.704
When I watch snow falling heavily

02:02.997 --> 02:04.582
or anything similar…

02:06.543 --> 02:07.377
I feel myself

02:08.920 --> 02:09.921
thinning out.

02:11.798 --> 02:12.632
You see,

02:13.925 --> 02:16.719
I'm the kind of person
who's entirely absorbed in myself.

02:17.762 --> 02:20.348
I want to cover the whole world with me.

02:21.141 --> 02:24.018
I want everyone to know my story.

02:25.395 --> 02:27.480
So I keep talking

02:27.564 --> 02:29.023
and talking.

02:29.107 --> 02:30.859
Then when it snows

02:30.942 --> 02:32.986
or when rain comes down in sheets,

02:33.653 --> 02:34.904
I thin out.

02:35.947 --> 02:38.783
But it's not a bad thing.

02:39.909 --> 02:43.079
A part of me
wants to cover the whole world with me,

02:43.872 --> 02:45.665
and a part of me wants to thin out.

02:47.250 --> 02:48.960
I think both exist in me.

02:58.386 --> 02:59.387
Inside me,

03:00.054 --> 03:03.016
there's Yeong-sil,
who wants to live an easygoing life,

03:03.600 --> 03:06.436
and there's Byeon Eun-a,
who wants to swing blades of revenge.

03:07.353 --> 03:08.187
Is it like that?

03:08.938 --> 03:09.772
That's right.

03:13.860 --> 03:15.361
"Thinning out."

03:17.113 --> 03:17.947
I like that phrase.

03:19.115 --> 03:20.033
Has your nosebleed

03:20.992 --> 03:22.035
thinned out?

03:22.994 --> 03:24.996
It disappeared a while ago.

03:27.165 --> 03:28.458
How's the weather today?

03:29.584 --> 03:31.085
Does it make you thin out?

03:32.754 --> 03:34.380
I'm thinning out severely.

03:35.840 --> 03:37.216
The traffic is terrible,

03:38.009 --> 03:40.053
so I'm completely stuck.

03:48.186 --> 03:49.479
I'm getting a call.

03:50.438 --> 03:51.689
I should answer it.

03:51.773 --> 03:53.775
Right, I'll hang up now.

03:54.609 --> 03:55.985
Be careful driving in the snow.

03:56.069 --> 03:57.111
I will.

04:07.997 --> 04:11.751
H-H-H-Hello?

04:11.834 --> 04:12.835
This is 911.

04:12.919 --> 04:17.006
-H-H-How far along a-a-are you?
-We're on our way.

04:17.090 --> 04:19.968
There was an accident on the way,
so we're taking a detour.

04:20.051 --> 04:20.885
You're okay, right?

04:21.386 --> 04:23.888
I-I-I-I'm… I'm really cold right now.

04:24.597 --> 04:26.724
-Can I turn on the engine?
-No, sir.

04:27.308 --> 04:28.977
Starting the car could cause a fire.

04:29.060 --> 04:30.436
-Curl up as tight as you can.
-Okay.

04:30.520 --> 04:32.522
Please hang in there. We'll be there soon.

04:32.605 --> 04:33.523
Look, I…

04:34.399 --> 04:35.441
I'm not…

04:36.234 --> 04:38.152
making these noises on purpose.

04:38.987 --> 04:41.781
My whole body is shaking on its own.

04:42.824 --> 04:45.451
How are my knees dancing like this?

04:46.577 --> 04:48.371
Are you sure…

04:49.789 --> 04:51.207
I can't turn on the engine?

04:51.791 --> 04:52.875
Okay, please hurry.

05:09.976 --> 05:11.561
Hello?

05:12.228 --> 05:14.314
Is anyone out there?

05:24.574 --> 05:27.493
BY MA JAE-YEONG, YEONG-SIL

05:34.334 --> 05:41.132
MA JAE-YEONG

05:41.758 --> 05:44.427
I-I-I-I can't…

05:44.510 --> 05:46.888
take a call right now.

05:47.513 --> 05:49.849
L-L-L-Let's talk later.

05:55.605 --> 05:56.898
Damn it.

06:07.116 --> 06:09.327
I added Byeon Eun-a's pseudonym
in the screenplay,

06:09.410 --> 06:12.872
so don't go around talking about it,
and keep your mouth shut.

06:12.955 --> 06:14.165
I'm warning you.

06:14.248 --> 06:16.751
If you go around running your mouth,
I won't just stand by.

06:18.795 --> 06:19.796
This little punk…

06:25.093 --> 06:27.220
-Yes?
-I know, you bastard!

06:27.303 --> 06:28.137
It's Yeong-sil!

06:28.721 --> 06:30.056
You rude bastard!

06:30.139 --> 06:32.266
What? "Keep your mouth shut"?

06:32.350 --> 06:34.060
Why do I have to keep my mouth shut?

06:34.143 --> 06:36.437
How am I supposed to do that?

06:36.521 --> 06:37.355
Hey!

06:38.064 --> 06:42.026
I've never kept my mouth shut in my life!

06:42.110 --> 06:44.695
What? What did you say?

06:44.779 --> 06:46.197
I'm not following.

06:46.280 --> 06:47.365
"I'm so sorry!"

06:47.990 --> 06:52.370
"Please forgive me for being a coward
and only listing her pseudonym!"

06:53.538 --> 06:54.497
You bastard!

06:54.580 --> 06:56.249
That's what you should've said, asshole!

06:57.875 --> 06:59.919
Why should I speak respectfully to you?

07:01.045 --> 07:02.672
Think about how you treated me.

07:03.422 --> 07:05.842
Do you know how much crap I took from you?

07:06.968 --> 07:08.678
I'm thankful for one thing, though.

07:09.512 --> 07:11.389
My blood boils whenever I think of you.

07:12.014 --> 07:14.267
It made me think,
"Damn it, I have to succeed

07:14.350 --> 07:17.645
so I can crush those worthless scumbags
and pathetic nobodies

07:17.728 --> 07:19.522
and shut them up for good."

07:21.315 --> 07:23.276
So I clenched my teeth
and fought my way to the top.

07:24.068 --> 07:24.986
The thing is,

07:25.903 --> 07:28.239
I know what kind of person you are.

07:29.240 --> 07:31.033
You want others to fail like you,

07:31.117 --> 07:32.577
so the second someone starts rising,

07:32.660 --> 07:35.663
you rip into them and drag them down.

07:37.540 --> 07:38.749
But guess what?

07:38.833 --> 07:40.460
Your words can't drag me down.

07:41.419 --> 07:42.628
But you can go ahead and try.

07:45.006 --> 07:45.923
Or how about this?

07:47.133 --> 07:49.385
Don't hold back and just come up here.

07:49.469 --> 07:53.264
I'll treat you with respect
when you do, okay?

07:56.976 --> 07:59.604
You don't even have the balls
to make it up here.

07:59.687 --> 08:01.606
I'm going to make it up there,
you bastard!

08:01.689 --> 08:03.900
Just wait, you son of a bitch!

08:05.943 --> 08:07.403
Just you wait!

09:12.510 --> 09:13.594
Sir!

09:13.678 --> 09:14.637
Are you okay?

09:15.263 --> 09:17.014
Kim, grab the gear!

09:19.559 --> 09:21.143
EMERGENCY SERVICES

09:24.188 --> 09:25.481
I'm hot.

09:25.565 --> 09:27.066
Sir, please lie down.

09:27.149 --> 09:28.025
Just lie down.

09:28.109 --> 09:29.360
But I'm really hot.

09:29.443 --> 09:30.945
-Hey, take his temperature.
-I'm hot.

09:31.028 --> 09:32.280
-Yes, sir.
-I'm hot.

09:52.216 --> 09:54.302
I almost died today.

09:54.385 --> 09:56.596
It snowed like crazy in Yangpyeong,

09:56.679 --> 09:57.888
and the car started skidding.

09:58.472 --> 09:59.307
Holy shit.

09:59.390 --> 10:01.017
It kept skidding in slow motion.

10:01.100 --> 10:02.518
Who knew slow motion was so scary?

10:04.562 --> 10:08.316
I was fighting for my life,
upside down in a -20° snowfield,

10:08.983 --> 10:11.110
when that asshole Ma Jae-yeong
pissed me off.

10:12.403 --> 10:15.239
I was determined to make it out alive.

10:16.115 --> 10:17.366
Everyone's asleep.

10:17.950 --> 10:19.368
Let's talk tomorrow.

10:20.119 --> 10:22.121
Go ahead and sleep.
You can read this in the morning.

10:22.204 --> 10:24.123
I have to finish what I was saying.

10:27.126 --> 10:29.712
I imagined an insanely hot summer day.

10:30.338 --> 10:31.464
I was super focused.

10:32.089 --> 10:35.301
I'm not lying when I say
that it made me sweat.

10:35.384 --> 10:36.761
I was sweating at -20°.

10:37.595 --> 10:39.096
I couldn't believe it actually worked.

10:39.180 --> 10:41.390
People can do things
when they're pushed to the limit.

10:42.016 --> 10:43.142
But you know what's even crazier?

10:45.645 --> 10:48.939
I must've imagined too hard
because I'm still sweating.

10:50.733 --> 10:53.027
I can't shut off this heat inside me.

10:56.322 --> 10:58.074
Hey, Dong-man!

10:58.741 --> 11:00.951
Hwang Dong-man!

11:01.035 --> 11:03.037
Let's move up!

11:03.996 --> 11:06.916
That damn bastard is at it again!

11:09.460 --> 11:11.003
You've got to be kidding me.

11:11.087 --> 11:13.255
He sent 300 messages.
You'd think a war broke out or something.

11:16.258 --> 11:17.802
Why can't he just send it all
in one long message?

11:17.885 --> 11:20.930
Why does he send them line by line?
It's a pain to delete them.

11:23.557 --> 11:24.517
Seriously.

11:24.600 --> 11:27.395
When can I finally stop hearing from him?

11:30.314 --> 11:33.609
When can I finally stop hearing you
talk crap about him while we eat?

11:34.568 --> 11:36.821
Whether it's 300 or 900 messages,

11:37.446 --> 11:39.448
just go, "Oh, he's at it again,"
and move on.

11:40.324 --> 11:42.076
I told you time and time again

11:42.159 --> 11:44.495
that anyone trashing an idiot
for being an idiot is an idiot too!

11:48.416 --> 11:49.917
Idiot best friends.

11:51.210 --> 11:52.211
You two won't split up.

11:53.379 --> 11:55.840
Ormy and Gasmy.

11:56.632 --> 11:59.468
Even your nicknames
come from the same cheap word.

11:59.552 --> 12:02.179
Do you know how hard I worked
to split you two up?

12:03.431 --> 12:04.807
You two are soulmates.

12:05.433 --> 12:06.600
You'll never split up.

12:09.520 --> 12:11.397
Just keep living like that.

12:12.523 --> 12:14.442
Keep talking crap about Hwang Dong-man,

12:15.317 --> 12:17.278
keep proving you're just like him,

12:18.529 --> 12:20.781
and keep living as his soulmate.

12:30.708 --> 12:32.042
You're saying this works?

12:32.126 --> 12:33.127
Good morning.

12:33.210 --> 12:34.670
-Good morning.
-Good morning, Ms. Ko.

12:35.671 --> 12:39.383
CEO KO HYE-JIN

12:45.473 --> 12:47.141
Good morning, Mr. Choi.

12:47.725 --> 12:50.978
I'm following up to see if the screenplay
I asked you to forward to Mr. Noh

12:51.061 --> 12:53.481
has been passed along.

12:54.064 --> 12:56.275
I apologize for messaging you
while you're busy,

12:56.358 --> 12:58.736
but I'm reaching out again
because it's urgent.

12:58.819 --> 13:03.157
It's imperative
that we cast him in this movie.

13:03.782 --> 13:05.034
The doors are opening.

13:09.121 --> 13:10.039
-Hi.
-Hello, sir.

13:10.122 --> 13:11.123
-Hello.
-Hello.

13:11.207 --> 13:12.249
Hi.

13:13.626 --> 13:14.502
Hey, Ax.

13:17.379 --> 13:19.173
Did you read the screenplay
sent from Kopark Film?

13:23.636 --> 13:25.054
-Yes.
-How is it?

13:27.306 --> 13:28.474
It's good.

13:29.308 --> 13:30.309
That's it?

13:31.769 --> 13:33.020
Do you not know how to elaborate?

13:34.980 --> 13:39.109
Should I pass this on or not?
Give it to me straight.

13:39.193 --> 13:40.694
Would Noh Kang-sik say yes?

13:40.778 --> 13:42.571
Or would he curse me out for this?

13:45.574 --> 13:46.534
I think it's a shame

13:47.743 --> 13:49.495
that a big company like ours
can't take part in it

13:50.162 --> 13:53.123
because it's a project
funded by the government.

13:53.207 --> 13:55.876
The storyline is genuinely terrifying
and completely blindsides you.

13:55.960 --> 13:58.045
There's no buildup and tension.

13:58.128 --> 14:00.464
It breaks all the basic rules of horror

14:01.257 --> 14:03.092
and pushes forward, full throttle.

14:03.717 --> 14:07.054
When it's released,
people will hesitate before opening doors,

14:07.137 --> 14:08.806
wondering what might be on the other side.

14:10.724 --> 14:12.726
It's the second-best screenplay
I've read this year.

14:13.686 --> 14:15.938
It'll blow the minds of veteran directors.

14:18.857 --> 14:19.733
Give it to me.

14:20.609 --> 14:22.319
Come on, give me the screenplay.

14:37.042 --> 14:38.419
Excuse me, Eun-a.

14:39.587 --> 14:40.504
Can we talk?

14:45.885 --> 14:48.137
Why did you agree to it?

14:49.305 --> 14:52.099
Why did you agree to Mr. Choi telling you
to drop out of my film?

14:52.182 --> 14:53.809
I'm not okay with it.

14:55.311 --> 14:58.105
You could've told him
that you'd discuss it with me first.

14:58.856 --> 14:59.940
Would that have worked?

15:01.066 --> 15:03.485
I enjoy watching people

15:04.111 --> 15:04.945
who walk all over me.

15:07.448 --> 15:08.532
I think to myself, "Just wait."

15:09.199 --> 15:10.993
"I'll make sure you end up embarrassed."

15:13.329 --> 15:15.039
I'm going to be very successful, you see.

15:15.873 --> 15:16.707
Very.

15:19.209 --> 15:21.003
CHEONGRAM WRITING ACADEMY

15:49.114 --> 15:50.991
Fix your printer already,

15:51.075 --> 15:53.869
instead of coming here all the time
to print out stuff.

15:53.953 --> 15:54.912
You know what?

15:55.663 --> 15:59.041
I'll still come here to teach
even after I debut and blow up.

16:00.751 --> 16:01.961
I won't change.

16:02.044 --> 16:04.630
It's fine if you change,
so please make it big.

16:04.713 --> 16:05.673
I'm begging you.

16:09.259 --> 16:12.221
KNOCK KNOCK KNOCK
BY MA JAE-YEONG, YEONG-SIL

16:16.141 --> 16:18.060
This screenplay is insane.

16:37.955 --> 16:40.374
You finally get to see the light of day.

16:47.047 --> 16:48.173
WOW, WHAT'S THAT?

16:50.718 --> 16:51.719
It's amazing, right?

16:52.302 --> 16:53.303
Tonight sound good?

16:54.680 --> 16:55.931
NODS

16:57.975 --> 16:58.809
CEO KO

17:01.770 --> 17:03.105
Hey, it's me.

17:03.188 --> 17:04.565
Keep a room open tonight.

17:05.482 --> 17:07.526
Noh Kang-sik will be coming.

17:08.110 --> 17:08.986
Tonight?

17:10.070 --> 17:11.280
Thank you.

17:12.489 --> 17:15.159
I was worried
I was bothering you too much.

17:15.784 --> 17:16.869
Thank you so much.

17:17.786 --> 17:19.747
Yes, I'll see you later.

17:35.721 --> 17:38.098
Jun-hwan, I have a favor to ask.

17:44.313 --> 17:45.898
Make sure Dong-man stays away

17:46.732 --> 17:47.691
from Agit today.

17:47.775 --> 17:48.776
Goddamn it.

17:48.859 --> 17:50.235
You're kidding me.

17:50.819 --> 17:51.737
What the heck?

17:51.820 --> 17:54.031
-Group chat!
-This is the group chat.

17:54.114 --> 17:55.657
-This is the group chat.
-Oh no. What do I do?

17:55.741 --> 17:56.575
THE EIGHT CLUB

17:57.201 --> 17:58.202
Where's "delete"?

17:58.285 --> 17:59.828
DELETE MESSAGE
DELETE FOR EVERYONE

17:59.912 --> 18:01.580
My goodness.

18:02.790 --> 18:05.334
THIS MESSAGE HAS BEEN DELETED

18:12.716 --> 18:14.551
WEATHER MAKER
BY HWANG DONG-MAN

18:14.635 --> 18:15.761
CEO KO HYE-JIN

18:17.137 --> 18:18.347
-Hello.
-Hello.

18:18.430 --> 18:19.681
So anyway…

18:19.765 --> 18:21.225
Noh Kang-sik is coming.

18:21.308 --> 18:23.393
She's trying to cast him
for Jae-yeong's film.

18:23.477 --> 18:24.561
Hello.

18:25.145 --> 18:27.856
And she knows
you're not on good terms with him.

18:29.900 --> 18:31.401
-Hello.
-Hello.

18:52.339 --> 18:57.010
Wow, losses from voice phishing
reach a trillion won a year.

18:57.094 --> 18:58.554
That's scary.

18:59.888 --> 19:01.431
Can I ask you a favor?

19:01.932 --> 19:02.933
Huh? What is it?

19:03.517 --> 19:04.643
You can say no.

19:05.644 --> 19:06.478
What is it?

19:09.439 --> 19:10.732
Would it be okay

19:11.650 --> 19:13.652
if I registered my grandma's address
at your place?

19:14.278 --> 19:15.404
What?

19:16.488 --> 19:17.614
Seriously, you can say no.

19:25.664 --> 19:26.623
Oh goodness.

19:29.459 --> 19:30.377
Let's go to the hospital.

19:30.460 --> 19:33.505
So what if I'm falling apart?

19:34.298 --> 19:37.342
If we can fix you before that happens,
we should get you fixed up.

19:37.426 --> 19:39.720
If we don't,
I'll have to carry you on my back.

19:39.803 --> 19:41.013
Don't be silly.

19:44.266 --> 19:46.393
You always carried me on your back.

19:47.394 --> 19:48.937
I was in elementary school,

19:49.897 --> 19:51.190
so why did you carry me around?

19:51.940 --> 19:53.901
I loved carrying kids on my back.

19:54.818 --> 19:57.821
It felt comforting
to feel warmth on my back.

19:59.406 --> 20:02.910
I wish I could've carried you on my back
when you were a baby.

20:06.246 --> 20:07.289
Yes?

20:08.874 --> 20:09.708
Two rolls of gimbap, please.

20:09.791 --> 20:10.667
-Okay.
-Okay.

20:17.466 --> 20:18.675
Here you go.

20:57.172 --> 20:58.590
-You're here.
-Hello.

21:02.219 --> 21:03.220
It's been a while.

21:03.303 --> 21:04.554
You're still as sexy as ever.

21:06.265 --> 21:07.307
Watch it.

21:09.810 --> 21:10.644
Where's Mr. Choi?

21:10.727 --> 21:12.688
-He'll be here in about ten minutes.
-Yes.

21:12.771 --> 21:14.439
Okay. Let's head inside.

21:19.236 --> 21:20.070
Thanks.

21:21.863 --> 21:22.698
Hey.

21:23.198 --> 21:26.243
What's wrong with movies
and dramas these days?

21:26.326 --> 21:27.369
They're boring.

21:29.121 --> 21:29.955
Is it just me?

21:30.956 --> 21:33.417
I hear even the editors
are losing their minds while editing

21:33.500 --> 21:34.543
because everything's boring.

21:36.128 --> 21:39.172
In the past, there were at least
a couple of fun releases every year.

21:39.256 --> 21:41.842
But now, everything feels factory-made

21:42.968 --> 21:44.261
and basically the same.

21:46.054 --> 21:47.306
How did this happen?

21:49.474 --> 21:51.018
Everyone is getting anxious.

21:52.728 --> 21:54.313
Don't get anxious.

21:54.896 --> 21:56.398
I miss movies

21:57.065 --> 21:59.568
where people talk normally.

22:03.363 --> 22:04.489
Is he here?

22:08.535 --> 22:09.369
Hey.

22:11.413 --> 22:12.247
Salute!

22:18.045 --> 22:18.879
What do you think?

22:18.962 --> 22:20.047
Amazing, right?

22:21.715 --> 22:22.924
Nice.

22:23.842 --> 22:25.427
Let's open it in an hour.

22:28.347 --> 22:29.723
It only takes an hour to read.

22:29.806 --> 22:31.391
Let's drink first and read after.

22:31.475 --> 22:32.768
KNOCK KNOCK KNOCK
BY MA JAE-YEONG, YEONG-SIL

22:32.851 --> 22:35.270
The title is really lame, right?

22:35.854 --> 22:37.606
But the content is really awesome.

22:37.689 --> 22:40.400
If you miss out on this,
you'll regret it forever.

22:40.484 --> 22:41.777
As soon as I read this…

22:43.236 --> 22:44.321
My heart's still pounding.

22:44.905 --> 22:47.949
I messaged you as soon as I read it
so that no one could snatch it up.

22:48.033 --> 22:50.118
There's never been a character like this
in South Korea,

22:50.202 --> 22:51.036
and there never will be.

22:51.119 --> 22:53.121
You'll thank me after you read it.

22:53.205 --> 22:54.790
Thank me?

22:55.832 --> 22:56.917
Just don't bow to me.

22:57.000 --> 22:58.001
Oh, please.

23:01.630 --> 23:05.342
Have I ever tricked you
with something like this?

23:14.810 --> 23:15.644
Where's the director?

23:17.062 --> 23:18.480
You didn't call Ma Jae-yeong?

23:18.563 --> 23:20.774
The director should be here!
Tell him to hurry over.

23:20.857 --> 23:21.942
Okay.

23:31.243 --> 23:32.244
It's me.

23:33.036 --> 23:33.870
Where are you?

23:39.251 --> 23:41.503
Hey, the meat is done. Eat some.

23:42.254 --> 23:44.256
Does Noh Kang-sik
still beat up younger actors?

23:44.339 --> 23:47.008
I heard when a junior acts well,
he takes them outside and beats them,

23:47.092 --> 23:48.802
then pressures the director
not to use that take.

23:48.885 --> 23:51.513
With so many people hit,
it's a miracle he hasn't been canceled.

23:51.596 --> 23:54.933
If a top-tier actor gets canceled,
then everyone is screwed.

23:55.016 --> 23:58.436
There's no one besides Noh Kang-sik
who can fill theaters these days.

23:58.979 --> 24:00.605
How did Ma Jae-yeong get so lucky?

24:00.689 --> 24:02.524
He's working with Noh Kang-sik
in his debut film.

24:10.907 --> 24:11.992
What am I going to do?

24:13.451 --> 24:14.995
I feel sick to my stomach.

24:15.745 --> 24:17.622
It really hurts.

24:17.706 --> 24:19.249
When someone does well,

24:19.875 --> 24:22.502
I really feel sick to my stomach.

24:24.671 --> 24:25.922
Jeez, my stomach.

24:26.590 --> 24:28.758
How can someone be so…

24:30.177 --> 24:31.303
one-dimensional?

24:31.386 --> 24:33.430
I can't believe your stomach hurts
when you're jealous.

24:33.513 --> 24:35.849
You punk, you were the same way
when we debuted.

24:35.932 --> 24:38.310
You practically
lived in the bathroom for days.

24:38.393 --> 24:39.728
We wouldn't care if we did well.

24:39.811 --> 24:41.521
Who here had a successful debut film?

24:41.605 --> 24:42.522
We all tanked.

24:42.606 --> 24:45.108
I'm even jealous that you tanked.

24:45.192 --> 24:47.360
I'm even jealous that you get slammed
for making a bad movie.

24:47.444 --> 24:50.363
Guys like me,
who've never been in the ring before,

24:50.447 --> 24:52.991
get jealous of stories
about getting slammed and tanking.

24:55.744 --> 24:56.578
I wish…

24:57.662 --> 24:59.831
I could get slammed too. Jeez, my stomach.

25:01.666 --> 25:03.501
You piss me off the most, you asshole.

25:03.585 --> 25:05.670
When everyone was debuting
one after another

25:05.754 --> 25:07.339
and only the two of us were left,

25:07.422 --> 25:11.635
we spent so many nights
trashing everyone in The Eight Club.

25:11.718 --> 25:12.928
You blew me off the second you debuted,

25:13.553 --> 25:14.679
along with the others.

25:14.763 --> 25:17.307
You still blow me off. Do you know that?

25:21.228 --> 25:23.104
-Hey, that's enough.
-I can't.

25:23.188 --> 25:24.564
I can't eat or drink anymore.

25:26.107 --> 25:27.275
Jeez, my stomach.

25:34.950 --> 25:36.243
Wait up. I'll drive you home.

25:36.326 --> 25:37.369
It's okay. I'll just go on my own.

25:37.953 --> 25:39.204
You said your stomach hurts!

25:46.461 --> 25:48.255
Did we commit a crime or something?

25:48.338 --> 25:51.591
Can we stop coddling
Hwang Dong-man already?

25:51.675 --> 25:54.552
Put yourself in his shoes, you punk.

25:54.636 --> 25:57.305
If you were the last one left
without debuting,

25:57.389 --> 25:59.307
wouldn't this situation sting?

26:00.016 --> 26:01.893
Even the junior he used to belittle

26:02.519 --> 26:04.312
is about to move ahead of him.

26:05.939 --> 26:07.357
He's experiencing

26:08.733 --> 26:11.695
the sorrow of the survivor,
you little jerk.

26:29.045 --> 26:30.213
-Welcome.
-It's fun.

26:30.297 --> 26:31.131
Hey.

26:32.215 --> 26:33.174
Hey!

27:24.768 --> 27:25.643
Knock, knock.

27:26.811 --> 27:27.645
Hey.

27:29.856 --> 27:30.899
Are you done reading?

27:31.566 --> 27:33.109
What do you think? It's amazing, right?

27:35.528 --> 27:38.156
How did I end up with a life like this?

27:39.824 --> 27:41.993
A life where I'm first to get
a good screenplay.

27:47.707 --> 27:48.958
Who's the director again?

27:49.959 --> 27:51.586
Hey, Director Ma!

27:51.669 --> 27:52.629
Come in.

27:53.630 --> 27:54.464
Introduce yourself.

27:57.175 --> 27:58.718
Nice to meet you.

27:58.802 --> 27:59.844
My name is Ma Jae-yeong.

28:03.098 --> 28:04.057
Nice to meet you.

28:05.809 --> 28:07.268
I can tell from a handshake

28:07.977 --> 28:09.854
whether you're a man of substance or not.

28:18.446 --> 28:19.406
Nicely done.

28:20.740 --> 28:22.033
Take a seat.

28:22.117 --> 28:22.951
Okay.

28:27.831 --> 28:29.290
Please let it slide today.

28:30.333 --> 28:32.085
Fighting won't get you two anywhere.

28:32.669 --> 28:34.671
One thing I'll give you is that

28:35.755 --> 28:37.590
you don't associate with indecent people.

28:38.591 --> 28:40.385
So why Ma Jae-yeong?

28:41.094 --> 28:43.096
Am I dating him or something?

28:44.723 --> 28:46.975
My revised draft turned out really well.

28:48.601 --> 28:51.104
I wanted to give it to you first,

28:51.730 --> 28:53.189
but I don't think I can do that

28:54.816 --> 28:56.025
with Ma Jae-yeong nearby.

28:58.194 --> 29:01.698
Dealing with two people who clash
means I won't die a natural death.

29:01.781 --> 29:04.117
Dealing with you and Park Gyeong-se
aged me by ten years back then.

29:05.785 --> 29:07.787
If I die,
you'll find holy relics in my remains.

29:07.871 --> 29:10.540
You know, I always take a backseat.

29:10.623 --> 29:13.668
Ten years ago,
I took a backseat to Park Gyeong-se.

29:13.752 --> 29:15.754
Now, I'm taking a backseat
to Ma Jae-yeong.

29:16.379 --> 29:17.297
Dong-man.

29:18.631 --> 29:20.133
Listen carefully to the facts.

29:21.342 --> 29:24.554
You both applied for the same grant,
but Ma Jae-yeong got it, and you didn't.

29:25.180 --> 29:27.599
The judges selected his screenplay
by unanimous decision.

29:28.308 --> 29:29.642
Do you want a list of the judges?

29:30.685 --> 29:31.644
Jae-yeong's screenplay

29:32.312 --> 29:33.438
is good.

29:34.272 --> 29:36.191
He didn't see anyone for years

29:36.274 --> 29:39.152
and clenched his teeth so hard
while writing that five fell out.

29:39.235 --> 29:41.237
You can tell he treated it
like his last chance

29:41.321 --> 29:42.280
and gave it his all.

29:43.740 --> 29:45.867
You're free to hate whoever you want,

29:46.743 --> 29:49.579
but don't ruin something
someone poured everything into.

29:50.622 --> 29:53.625
-It'll end in a killing.
-Yeong-sil probably wrote it!

29:54.501 --> 29:56.127
Not that I know who Yeong-sil is.

29:57.587 --> 30:00.340
-Recognizing talent is also a talent.
-I see.

30:01.299 --> 30:04.010
Like the way Gyeong-se leans on you?

30:06.137 --> 30:09.015
I was just as good as Gyeong-se.

30:09.098 --> 30:11.851
If you had backed me
the way you backed Gyeong-se,

30:12.852 --> 30:14.312
I would've made it already.

30:16.564 --> 30:18.024
Aren't you embarrassed

30:18.107 --> 30:19.901
that people trash his films?

30:19.984 --> 30:21.986
Why, that little…

30:22.570 --> 30:23.404
You know what?

30:24.656 --> 30:26.282
I respect Park Gyeong-se.

30:28.618 --> 30:29.828
He keeps writing

30:30.453 --> 30:31.412
and keeps creating.

30:32.330 --> 30:34.207
He takes the ridicule and keeps going.

30:34.833 --> 30:37.335
He cries for days
with tears and snot running down his face.

30:37.418 --> 30:39.629
Then he steps into the ring again.

30:39.712 --> 30:40.839
He gets pummeled again, thinking,

30:40.922 --> 30:44.133
"Maybe one day,
I'll be able to fight for real and win."

30:44.217 --> 30:47.303
He gets his ass kicked
but keeps getting back into the ring.

30:48.096 --> 30:50.390
You think people only watch movies, right?

30:50.473 --> 30:51.891
They see and sense energy too and think,

30:51.975 --> 30:55.144
"Wow, he's really trying to
see this through to the end."

30:57.438 --> 30:58.273
But you?

31:00.066 --> 31:01.067
You won't make it to the end.

31:04.487 --> 31:05.446
From now on,

31:06.281 --> 31:07.866
don't trash Park Gyeong-se in front of me.

31:33.474 --> 31:35.226
Hey, you know what?

31:35.310 --> 31:37.812
-I can die happy today.
-Good.

31:37.896 --> 31:39.731
I have you by my side.

31:40.607 --> 31:42.025
Good, good.

31:42.108 --> 31:43.610
-Thank you so much, Kang-sik!
-Not at all.

31:45.278 --> 31:46.487
I'm heading out.

31:46.571 --> 31:47.405
-Good night.
-Take this.

31:47.488 --> 31:48.615
Thank you.

31:50.241 --> 31:51.200
Hello.

31:55.872 --> 31:58.082
Can I get a handshake?

31:58.625 --> 32:02.211
Please shake my hand once
and see what I'm like.

32:07.717 --> 32:08.718
Okay.

32:14.140 --> 32:15.183
Relax your grip.

32:15.934 --> 32:17.310
Do you always shake hands like this?

32:22.649 --> 32:24.400
Wait, wait, I give up.

32:24.484 --> 32:25.401
My wrist!

32:25.485 --> 32:26.361
Wait a second!

32:30.448 --> 32:32.033
Build your core strength.

32:35.870 --> 32:36.829
I'm off.

32:36.913 --> 32:38.456
-Get home safely!
-Thanks.

32:43.044 --> 32:44.087
Good night!

32:49.801 --> 32:50.969
Jeez.

32:52.720 --> 32:54.681
Learn some restraint.

32:54.764 --> 32:57.684
How can someone not know when to refrain?

32:57.767 --> 32:58.768
Please refrain!

33:00.228 --> 33:02.271
From giving me a lecture.

33:02.355 --> 33:03.648
That idiot.

33:04.232 --> 33:06.734
If you keep that up,
you'll be attending your own funeral!

33:11.322 --> 33:14.784
There should be lines
that make an actor come alive,

33:15.368 --> 33:17.161
but I didn't see a single one.

33:18.705 --> 33:19.789
All right.

33:19.872 --> 33:21.499
Try revising it one more time.

33:36.931 --> 33:37.890
Let's hear it.

33:39.225 --> 33:41.894
Why are you refusing the money
and the house?

33:41.978 --> 33:43.813
I changed my grandmother's address.

33:44.897 --> 33:46.899
Even if reporters find out about her,

33:47.525 --> 33:48.818
they won't come to our home.

33:48.901 --> 33:49.902
So what?

33:50.820 --> 33:52.405
You're just going to keep living there?

33:53.281 --> 33:54.574
Even if the chances are slim

33:55.158 --> 33:58.244
that people find out you're my daughter…

34:00.329 --> 34:03.708
I'm asking you to live in a way
that won't make me look bad.

34:03.791 --> 34:05.501
Is it just that
you don't want to do it for me?

34:05.585 --> 34:07.712
Do you just want me to catch backlash?

34:08.296 --> 34:09.547
I'm not asking for anything difficult.

34:10.048 --> 34:13.634
Everyone would love to have a nice house
and nice clothes.

34:14.927 --> 34:17.305
And while we're at it,
you might as well date a more decent guy.

34:17.388 --> 34:19.849
Hwang Dong-man is a decent man.

34:24.228 --> 34:25.229
By your standards.

34:25.313 --> 34:26.773
Of course, I'd date someone
based on my standards.

34:26.856 --> 34:28.399
Do you expect me to date someone
based on yours?

34:28.483 --> 34:30.234
What's so decent about him?

34:30.318 --> 34:31.360
I'm curious.

34:33.738 --> 34:34.739
What makes him decent?

34:36.157 --> 34:37.784
I feel safe with him.

34:38.910 --> 34:41.996
He'd be crying in pain,
then shake it off and bounce back.

34:44.457 --> 34:45.416
It hits me.

34:47.251 --> 34:49.504
"Oh, it's possible
to bounce back like that."

34:50.505 --> 34:51.923
"But why am I still struggling…

34:53.925 --> 34:55.593
with what happened in the past?"

35:02.183 --> 35:03.559
Watching him gives me strength

35:04.310 --> 35:07.396
and gives me hope
that I can bounce back like that one day.

35:09.148 --> 35:10.900
I'm not sure that day
will ever come, though.

35:13.402 --> 35:16.405
Giving me money
and dictating how I spend it

35:17.031 --> 35:18.032
is crossing the line.

35:18.658 --> 35:19.909
Do you think I need clothes?

35:21.661 --> 35:24.372
My grandma's the one who saved me
when I was barely hanging on.

35:25.706 --> 35:28.167
After Dad died, I got nosebleeds,
fearing I'd be abandoned again.

35:29.627 --> 35:30.795
She'd tell me, "I'm not going anywhere."

35:32.296 --> 35:33.339
"I won't leave you."

35:35.341 --> 35:37.844
She reassured me
while she fed and clothed me.

35:39.387 --> 35:41.639
When I have money,
I'm going to treat her to good food.

35:43.432 --> 35:45.226
If there's a machine
that'll make her healthy,

35:45.309 --> 35:47.478
I'll sell everything I own
to put her in that machine.

35:49.689 --> 35:51.190
If I can spend your money like that,
I'll take it.

35:56.070 --> 35:58.114
Go ahead. Spend it as you wish.

36:09.959 --> 36:12.295
You think your past is some kind of
badge of honor?

36:12.378 --> 36:14.172
You think your pain
is something to flaunt about?

36:21.804 --> 36:23.848
What about the nine-year-old Oh Jeong-hui,

36:23.931 --> 36:26.350
who grew up in a family
that bought rice in plastic bags

36:26.434 --> 36:28.769
and once stood crying under the eaves
after one burst in the rain,

36:28.853 --> 36:30.646
unable to go home?

36:31.230 --> 36:32.565
What if her first memory

36:32.648 --> 36:36.444
is of her drunk father
slamming a kitchen knife into the table?

36:38.613 --> 36:40.573
I've never said anything like this before.

36:42.033 --> 36:44.535
I hate even the thought
of bringing this up.

36:45.453 --> 36:47.747
What is it to you
that you cherish it so much?

36:47.830 --> 36:50.249
You act as if it's a precious memory!

36:54.253 --> 36:55.129
Pain?

36:57.506 --> 36:59.217
Do you know what real pain is?

37:05.723 --> 37:08.142
It's when your dad
went back to his first love!

37:41.050 --> 37:42.218
Should we get going?

38:02.905 --> 38:04.573
What did Ms. Ko Hye-jin say?

38:04.657 --> 38:05.866
Did she read your screenplay?

38:07.576 --> 38:08.703
I didn't give it to her.

38:10.705 --> 38:11.831
Why not?

38:12.456 --> 38:13.332
She said she won't work with me.

38:15.376 --> 38:16.210
Why?

38:20.089 --> 38:22.133
She said she can't handle
two people who clash.

38:23.426 --> 38:24.552
You see,

38:25.177 --> 38:26.887
I'm not on good terms with Ma Jae-yeong.

38:34.979 --> 38:35.813
Is it okay

38:36.564 --> 38:37.398
if I talk trash?

38:42.194 --> 38:43.529
Yeong-sil, you little brat.

38:47.491 --> 38:49.410
Why did you pour everything into it?

38:49.493 --> 38:53.205
Do talented people just dump their talent
anywhere without holding back?

38:53.289 --> 38:55.166
Do ideas just keep coming?

38:56.125 --> 38:58.461
Why did you waste your talent
on a jerk like him?

38:59.045 --> 39:00.796
Why are you letting that jerk use you?

39:02.715 --> 39:04.091
That's why you get nosebleeds.

39:09.764 --> 39:10.598
I'm sorry.

39:19.607 --> 39:20.983
I'm sorry.

39:21.734 --> 39:23.152
I'm really sorry.

39:23.736 --> 39:25.654
I think I lost my mind for a second.

39:25.738 --> 39:28.115
Wait, Eun-a.

39:28.199 --> 39:29.283
I'm so sorry.

39:29.950 --> 39:30.951
Eun-a.

39:37.583 --> 39:39.168
Do you hold back when you date someone?

39:40.544 --> 39:42.463
Is that how you've been dating people?

39:43.422 --> 39:44.924
If you get used, then so be it.

39:45.841 --> 39:47.718
Do you set a daily limit on getting used?

39:48.302 --> 39:51.972
You should give everything you can
and then more, even if it kills you!

39:59.480 --> 40:00.356
Eun-a.

40:35.683 --> 40:36.725
Hello?

40:38.853 --> 40:40.312
Tell me a funny story.

40:50.156 --> 40:51.365
Thank you.

40:58.998 --> 41:00.916
I know you have one.

41:02.084 --> 41:04.211
Why didn't you tell me about the accident?

41:06.714 --> 41:08.007
Because I wanted to be cool.

41:09.633 --> 41:12.761
If that were my last call with you,

41:14.013 --> 41:15.389
I wanted to be cool.

41:52.426 --> 41:53.469
What do you think?

41:57.056 --> 41:58.098
The moment

41:59.808 --> 42:01.602
you start using words like

42:02.561 --> 42:04.230
"death," "grief," or "pain" in a poem,

42:04.772 --> 42:06.065
it's no good.

42:15.533 --> 42:19.245
Since you absolutely refuse
to give a lecture,

42:19.328 --> 42:21.205
they asked me to arrange a meal with you.

42:22.873 --> 42:24.667
They all say they're your fans, Jin-man.

42:24.750 --> 42:26.585
Come on, help me save face.

42:40.099 --> 42:42.810
We've heard so much from the professor.

42:42.893 --> 42:45.229
He said you were unrivaled in grad school.

42:45.312 --> 42:47.856
People who write good poetry

42:47.940 --> 42:50.609
usually struggle to write a good thesis,

42:50.693 --> 42:52.611
but he said yours was exceptional.

42:53.237 --> 42:55.281
Why aren't you writing?

42:55.906 --> 42:58.576
Many people are waiting
for your poetry book.

43:02.913 --> 43:06.041
I like your poems because they're simple.

43:06.125 --> 43:08.002
They're simple, but powerful.

43:08.627 --> 43:12.089
It makes me wonder
how something so simple can hit so deeply.

43:13.007 --> 43:14.425
It's not actually simple.

43:14.508 --> 43:17.136
When it's carefully refined,
it just feels natural.

43:18.262 --> 43:20.931
My poem goes downhill
the moment I start polishing it.

43:21.015 --> 43:22.349
It's not as good as the first.

43:23.392 --> 43:26.103
How do you get good at refining writing?

43:29.189 --> 43:31.692
Have you seen Hwang Sol-mae's latest book?

43:31.775 --> 43:34.361
His poetry reminds me of yours,
Mr. Hwang.

43:34.445 --> 43:36.155
They're simple and straightforward.

43:36.655 --> 43:40.117
That kind of poetry isn't simple.
It's just bad.

43:40.200 --> 43:43.537
I can't believe poetry books like that
sell tens of thousands of copies.

43:44.705 --> 43:47.499
I heard you read
the entire dictionary three times.

43:47.583 --> 43:50.210
Can you tell me which one it is?

43:50.836 --> 43:52.463
There are so many publishers, you see.

43:53.839 --> 43:54.757
What's your purpose?

43:56.508 --> 43:59.845
What's your purpose in going as far as
reading a whole dictionary to write?

44:00.554 --> 44:02.598
Well, obviously,

44:02.681 --> 44:05.059
it's to write good poetry.

44:05.142 --> 44:07.478
I said purpose, not goal.

44:08.604 --> 44:10.105
What comes after, "You wrote well"?

44:11.023 --> 44:13.567
Is there really a purpose in this?

44:13.651 --> 44:16.070
You just write because you want to,

44:16.153 --> 44:18.238
the way you eat when you're hungry.

44:19.573 --> 44:22.701
You eat because if you don't, you'll die.

44:24.036 --> 44:25.162
Will you die if you don't write?

44:30.959 --> 44:32.044
You can't write a diary

44:33.754 --> 44:35.923
unless you can imagine

44:37.174 --> 44:39.343
someone reading it someday.

44:39.426 --> 44:41.011
It's the hope of being read.

44:42.513 --> 44:46.892
All writing begins
with the hope of being read.

44:47.893 --> 44:48.811
That disgusting hope…

44:50.562 --> 44:52.106
to be seen.

44:54.817 --> 44:56.652
I know a poet…

45:02.491 --> 45:03.951
who lost their child

45:05.702 --> 45:06.995
and turned to alcohol.

45:08.956 --> 45:11.166
One day, a brilliant line of poetry
came to them,

45:11.250 --> 45:13.043
and they scribbled it down on paper.

45:14.002 --> 45:15.546
That's how the poet came to write

45:15.629 --> 45:18.424
what critics still consider
their best poem.

45:19.883 --> 45:21.093
But afterward…

45:23.095 --> 45:24.721
they quit writing poetry.

45:27.724 --> 45:29.351
Their child was gone…

45:31.979 --> 45:35.566
yet they got excited
over a brilliant line of poetry,

45:36.483 --> 45:37.651
and it disgusted them.

45:43.073 --> 45:44.491
That's beautiful.

45:47.536 --> 45:48.454
What's beautiful?

45:49.997 --> 45:51.248
Which part do you find beautiful?

45:51.832 --> 45:55.252
Their child is gone, and they get excited
over a line of poetry?

45:55.335 --> 45:56.920
How is that beautiful?!

46:03.927 --> 46:04.761
Jin-man!

46:06.346 --> 46:08.015
I'll drive you back.

46:08.640 --> 46:09.475
Jin-man!

46:19.651 --> 46:23.739
On clear days, I remember the words,
"I'll come and get you"

46:25.032 --> 46:26.325
A child and their mother

46:27.242 --> 46:28.494
A dog and its owner

46:29.244 --> 46:30.621
A window filling with light

46:33.248 --> 46:34.333
It's Sunday

46:35.250 --> 46:36.835
People pass by

46:38.003 --> 46:40.005
I hope they're on their way
To pick someone up

46:40.797 --> 46:43.175
Or on their way to meet someone

46:47.429 --> 46:48.472
Because they're two different places

46:49.097 --> 46:51.058
Because it'll be different from this place

46:52.226 --> 46:53.393
I believe they are

47:05.239 --> 47:06.406
How much was it again?

47:07.032 --> 47:08.367
The money you got from the KFA.

47:08.909 --> 47:09.743
Three billion won.

47:11.662 --> 47:12.829
That's not much.

47:14.122 --> 47:15.249
Return it.

47:16.166 --> 47:17.000
Excuse me?

47:17.584 --> 47:18.544
Just return

47:19.503 --> 47:20.504
that money.

47:22.756 --> 47:23.757
Ms. Ko.

47:25.259 --> 47:26.552
Let's produce this ourselves.

47:27.135 --> 47:28.929
We'll bring in a top-tier cast,

47:29.012 --> 47:31.390
lock it in as a tentpole
for the second half of next year,

47:31.473 --> 47:32.933
and scale it big

47:33.559 --> 47:34.643
to cash in big.

47:35.519 --> 47:39.565
I'll guarantee at least triple the profit
Kopark Film would make going solo.

47:40.899 --> 47:42.901
This is so sudden.

47:44.361 --> 47:46.196
What would we tell the KFA?

47:46.280 --> 47:48.031
We can make up some excuse.

47:49.324 --> 47:51.577
Maybe say the director
decided to back out or something.

47:52.744 --> 47:55.998
If I fall out with the KFA,
I'll never get government-funded projects.

47:56.957 --> 48:00.252
Come on, why are you trying to
survive off something like that?

48:00.335 --> 48:04.172
You're looking at a deal that could
wipe out your debt and get you a building,

48:04.256 --> 48:07.175
so why are you aiming small,

48:07.259 --> 48:09.219
especially when you always
worry about payroll?

48:11.138 --> 48:12.556
Is this about moral purity?

48:13.557 --> 48:14.766
It's time for Kopark Film

48:15.934 --> 48:16.852
to level up.

48:17.644 --> 48:19.354
I'll take you to the next level.

48:20.230 --> 48:21.315
We'll split the profits

48:21.398 --> 48:23.400
nine to one.

48:24.776 --> 48:27.029
The one I'm carving out for you

48:27.112 --> 48:31.074
will be worth far more than anything
Kopark Film would pull in solo.

48:31.158 --> 48:32.242
I guarantee it!

48:35.621 --> 48:37.497
The thought alone makes you smile, right?

48:38.123 --> 48:38.957
Let's be honest.

48:41.043 --> 48:42.044
What have you done?

48:42.127 --> 48:44.504
Ma Jae-yeong worked his ass off
to win the grant,

48:44.588 --> 48:48.091
and he chose your company,
so you got everything handed to you.

48:49.301 --> 48:50.260
I think…

48:51.178 --> 48:52.346
we'll take it from here.

48:53.305 --> 48:54.514
And we don't need Noh Kang-sik.

48:54.598 --> 48:56.058
The director said he'd work with me.

48:59.186 --> 49:00.479
Of course, I'd choose Kopark Film.

49:01.855 --> 49:03.023
I'm excited to be here.

49:04.149 --> 49:07.611
When I asked how he felt about
working with Choi Film instead…

49:09.529 --> 49:11.490
he said he'd be grateful.

49:12.741 --> 49:15.410
Look, the odds are already
stacked against you.

49:15.494 --> 49:16.995
Just take my offer.

49:17.954 --> 49:19.247
I'll make you money.

49:20.248 --> 49:22.376
Let's make some money, Pro Ko!

49:29.132 --> 49:30.133
All right.

49:33.929 --> 49:37.140
I'm sure you've heard
that I started out as a journalist.

49:37.724 --> 49:38.725
Yes, of course.

49:38.809 --> 49:42.187
I wasn't sure I could make it in film,
so I started as a broadcast journalist.

49:43.480 --> 49:45.148
During my probation period,

49:45.232 --> 49:47.984
I had to hunt for stories everywhere,
including police stations.

49:49.528 --> 49:50.612
There was a day

49:51.238 --> 49:52.781
when I couldn't find anything.

49:53.448 --> 49:56.576
When I called to say there was nothing,
my boss asked,

49:57.327 --> 49:59.621
"Where are you?
What do you see right now?"

50:00.956 --> 50:01.873
I said, "A university hospital."

50:02.499 --> 50:04.626
They told me to go inside, so I did.

50:05.252 --> 50:06.670
And they said,
"Go inside the funeral hall."

50:07.295 --> 50:08.380
"Who died?"

50:09.506 --> 50:11.383
I said, "They're all ordinary people."

50:11.466 --> 50:13.510
Then my boss asked,
"Do you see any unusual deaths?"

50:14.803 --> 50:16.346
There was one young child.

50:16.930 --> 50:19.015
And they said, "Go inside."

50:19.599 --> 50:23.228
"Go inside and ask the parents
how the kid died."

50:27.566 --> 50:30.444
I started swearing.

50:31.903 --> 50:34.364
"I said I can't do it,
you fucking bastard!"

50:35.157 --> 50:36.908
"I won't do this shit, asshole."

50:38.118 --> 50:39.494
"I'm going to do something fun."

50:40.120 --> 50:41.997
"Something really fun."

50:42.873 --> 50:46.460
"I'm going to make something so fun
even grieving parents will be

50:46.543 --> 50:48.920
doubled over laughing, you bastard!"

50:53.675 --> 50:54.593
And then

50:55.802 --> 50:57.012
I quit.

51:00.348 --> 51:02.476
I joined this industry
to do something fun,

51:03.810 --> 51:07.147
but the same kind of scumbag is here,
like at the news desk back then.

51:11.693 --> 51:13.028
I'm going to live a fun life.

51:13.904 --> 51:16.865
And I'm cutting ties with you,
you dirty scumbag.

51:18.366 --> 51:19.868
You can have it all.

51:20.452 --> 51:21.578
Knock yourself out.

51:26.208 --> 51:27.584
Come on, Ms. Ko.

51:27.667 --> 51:30.212
You can't do business
by acting on your feelings.

51:37.886 --> 51:41.056
My grandmother used to say
cooking while angry makes food taste bad.

51:42.057 --> 51:45.393
She always pressed her palms together
before cooking.

51:52.734 --> 51:55.320
When she was feeling good,
she'd grab a radish from the garden

51:55.403 --> 51:57.614
and whip together a soup.

51:57.697 --> 52:00.450
And it was delicious
even though it was a simple recipe!

52:00.534 --> 52:01.576
Feelings?

52:01.660 --> 52:02.994
They matter!

52:03.078 --> 52:04.913
I make movies with that in mind,

52:04.996 --> 52:06.832
so people watching feel good too!

52:13.588 --> 52:15.131
Thank you for everything.

52:17.551 --> 52:19.553
You have a long way to go.

52:19.636 --> 52:22.222
That temper of yours
is why you can't make money.

52:23.181 --> 52:25.976
Who the hell in this country
goes into filmmaking to make money?

52:26.059 --> 52:27.477
You do it for fun!

53:11.897 --> 53:13.356
After quitting,

53:13.982 --> 53:15.942
I went home and bawled.

53:16.735 --> 53:18.570
Then I got a text from Park Gyeong-se.

53:20.697 --> 53:22.115
He sent me a screenplay

53:23.700 --> 53:24.618
and asked me to read it.

53:24.701 --> 53:26.620
I sent you a screenplay. Can you read it?

53:30.498 --> 53:31.917
The screenplay I read

53:33.335 --> 53:34.753
was The Lustful Bottle Opener.

53:50.518 --> 53:52.562
THE LUSTFUL BOTTLE OPENER

53:54.814 --> 53:56.107
Then I called him and said…

53:57.984 --> 53:58.818
Gyeong-se.

54:03.990 --> 54:04.908
I love you.

54:07.953 --> 54:10.080
When you see something really good,

54:11.539 --> 54:14.793
the words "I love you" just slip out.

54:17.003 --> 54:19.005
What happened to the man

54:20.298 --> 54:22.133
who used to write words…

54:25.428 --> 54:27.514
that could make a crying woman…

54:29.641 --> 54:31.059
burst into laughter?

54:33.436 --> 54:35.605
That man is dead.

55:18.773 --> 55:21.526
So what's the best screenplay
you've read this year?

55:25.030 --> 55:27.449
You said Knock knock knock
was the second-best.

55:28.700 --> 55:29.534
So what's the best?

55:30.660 --> 55:32.162
Weather Maker.

55:32.746 --> 55:33.872
What maker?

55:35.540 --> 55:36.499
Weather.

55:37.125 --> 55:38.334
The one by Director Hwang Dong-man.

55:44.090 --> 55:45.925
Goodness gracious.

55:46.009 --> 55:47.302
The revision turned out well.

55:47.969 --> 55:49.846
It's on a whole new level
from the first draft.

55:51.347 --> 55:52.390
Listen carefully.

55:53.224 --> 55:55.769
There are many types of abilities.

55:55.852 --> 55:59.481
A director with an amazing blueprint
can have so-so results.

55:59.564 --> 56:03.151
A director with a so-so blueprint
can bring decent results.

56:03.234 --> 56:04.736
Now, what does this mean?

56:05.737 --> 56:08.573
It means writing isn't even one-tenth
of a director's abilities.

56:09.157 --> 56:11.451
What matters most
is the ability to deliver.

56:11.534 --> 56:16.081
Someone who can handle 200 unruly people,
grit their teeth, and hit the finish line.

56:17.874 --> 56:19.667
Why launch a ship that's going to sink?

56:19.751 --> 56:20.585
First floor.

56:20.668 --> 56:21.503
Jeez.

56:22.378 --> 56:24.297
I'm the only one who's kind enough
to tell you this.

56:25.840 --> 56:27.175
I'm teaching you a lot.

56:40.522 --> 56:42.899
Hey, Hwang Dong-man.

56:42.982 --> 56:45.610
I saw you took a nice crap online.

56:46.236 --> 56:47.487
What was it again?

56:47.570 --> 56:52.158
"Exposing Choi Film's exploitation
of small, powerless production companies."

56:52.242 --> 56:55.453
If you did something wrong,
you have to accept the backlash.

57:04.337 --> 57:07.090
You know what incompetent people
in this field have in common?

57:08.133 --> 57:09.050
It's that

57:10.218 --> 57:11.719
they don't even consider

57:12.679 --> 57:14.389
that this might not be their path.

57:14.472 --> 57:16.975
Capable people
think about it countless times.

57:17.058 --> 57:19.936
But incompetent people don't.

57:20.019 --> 57:22.689
Why? Because they've never
had to stake their lives on anything.

57:23.273 --> 57:28.486
Only people who have pushed themselves
to their limits and truly faced them

57:29.112 --> 57:30.405
can say the words,

57:31.281 --> 57:33.324
"Maybe this isn't my path."

57:33.408 --> 57:34.659
Am I wrong?

57:34.742 --> 57:38.746
People like you
who spend their lives just dabbling…

57:40.457 --> 57:41.666
Whatever.

57:41.749 --> 57:45.336
Even if your path is long and rough,
keep dabbling your way through it.

57:46.546 --> 57:47.464
A few days ago,

57:48.298 --> 57:49.757
something happened to me.

57:49.841 --> 57:52.802
Man, I'm bored already.
Do I have to listen to this?

57:52.886 --> 57:54.971
I listened to you, so now it's your turn.

57:55.597 --> 57:58.725
My car flipped over on a snowy road,
and I couldn't get out.

57:58.808 --> 58:00.768
I couldn't even turn on the engine
because I was afraid it might explode,

58:00.852 --> 58:02.228
so I just sat there shivering.

58:02.312 --> 58:04.439
And then I imagined
a scorching hot summer day.

58:04.522 --> 58:06.816
I'd read somewhere that it works,

58:06.900 --> 58:08.193
and it actually did.

58:08.776 --> 58:10.820
Even at -20°, I was sweating.

58:11.821 --> 58:15.116
As you can see, I'm still sweating.

58:15.200 --> 58:16.284
Go see a doctor.

58:16.367 --> 58:19.537
But I often catch myself
practicing acceptance speeches.

58:19.621 --> 58:21.164
I don't do it on purpose.

58:21.247 --> 58:25.418
It happens while I'm brushing my teeth
or riding the bus.

58:25.502 --> 58:29.339
If I'm still sweating
from briefly imagining something,

58:29.422 --> 58:31.674
will the acceptance speech
I've practiced for 20 years

58:31.758 --> 58:33.885
just scatter like dust in the wind?

58:35.595 --> 58:37.096
You're really messed up.

58:37.764 --> 58:40.642
You should see a psychiatrist
while you're at the hospital.

58:40.725 --> 58:42.685
And delete that post
if you don't want to get sued.

58:42.769 --> 58:44.229
I'm not deleting it.

58:44.312 --> 58:45.730
Delete it, you idiot!

58:47.565 --> 58:50.401
You're practicing acceptance speeches
for when you get famous,

58:51.110 --> 58:53.029
and you post crap like that online?

58:53.112 --> 58:54.781
You can get canceled over an old post.

58:54.864 --> 58:55.823
Delete it, you idiot.

58:55.907 --> 58:57.825
I did it because nobody else can!

58:58.826 --> 59:02.080
I did it because everyone's afraid
of a piece of trash like him!

59:03.957 --> 59:07.043
You punk, I've had enough of this.

59:07.126 --> 59:08.253
"A piece of trash"?

59:28.106 --> 59:29.274
Who wants napa cabbage?

59:39.909 --> 59:40.743
Is he a thug?

59:46.124 --> 59:47.500
Jeez.

59:50.587 --> 59:51.421
Your trunk.

59:52.714 --> 59:53.756
I'm good, thanks.

59:53.840 --> 59:54.799
Open it.

59:56.050 --> 59:57.260
I live alone, so no thanks.

59:57.343 --> 59:58.720
I said open it.

01:00:12.984 --> 01:00:13.901
Take two.

01:00:24.871 --> 01:00:26.414
-That's it.
-That's it?

01:00:31.461 --> 01:00:32.629
-What? 20 billion won?
-Yeah.

01:00:32.712 --> 01:00:35.673
Jeez, what's the break-even point, then?

01:00:36.924 --> 01:00:40.261
Why would you invest so much money
in a piece of crap like that?

01:00:40.345 --> 01:00:42.180
It has no substance.

01:00:43.097 --> 01:00:47.101
They're doing everything they can
to cover it up with mise-en-scène.

01:00:47.185 --> 01:00:49.687
My goodness.

01:00:49.771 --> 01:00:52.190
Now, mise-en-scène sucks too.

01:00:53.608 --> 01:00:57.695
And there isn't a single heartfelt line.

01:00:57.779 --> 01:01:02.700
It's like the writer racked their brains
and desperately forced out some words.

01:01:02.784 --> 01:01:03.618
Jeez.

01:01:03.701 --> 01:01:05.828
Hey, say something to Director An.

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:07.205
Does anyone tell him this?

01:01:07.288 --> 01:01:08.373
You two are friends, right?

01:01:08.456 --> 01:01:09.707
Tell him already!

01:01:10.458 --> 01:01:13.628
This is why
I plaster the internet with posts.

01:01:13.711 --> 01:01:15.296
It's because no one says anything!

01:01:16.089 --> 01:01:17.048
I'm sorry.

01:01:17.131 --> 01:01:19.342
The other company
already persuaded the director,

01:01:19.967 --> 01:01:21.386
so there's nothing I can do.

01:01:21.969 --> 01:01:23.680
I'll have to return the grant.

01:01:25.181 --> 01:01:28.935
There's an option to move forward
with the runner-up's screenplay.

01:01:29.018 --> 01:01:31.396
If the winner declines the grant,

01:01:31.479 --> 01:01:35.692
we can award it to the runner-up,
and there are no procedural issues.

01:01:36.651 --> 01:01:38.986
Would you like to read their screenplay?

01:01:39.987 --> 01:01:41.948
It's called Weather Maker.

01:01:43.866 --> 01:01:47.161
Stop overdoing it
with visual effects and whatnot

01:01:47.245 --> 01:01:49.330
and focus more on the props!

01:01:49.414 --> 01:01:51.290
What if the actor suddenly opens a drawer?

01:01:51.374 --> 01:01:53.418
It could happen, right?

01:01:53.501 --> 01:01:55.795
WEATHER MAKER

01:02:03.970 --> 01:02:04.804
What do you think?

01:02:06.556 --> 01:02:07.765
There's a lot going on.

01:02:10.518 --> 01:02:11.811
Do you think it'll make its money back?

01:02:13.730 --> 01:02:15.064
I understand your concern.

01:02:17.191 --> 01:02:19.068
Then let's just drop it.

01:02:20.820 --> 01:02:21.779
Okay.

01:02:21.863 --> 01:02:24.741
For the love of god,
stuff the drawers on set!

01:02:24.824 --> 01:02:27.368
Who lives in a house with empty drawers?

01:02:37.253 --> 01:02:38.129
You know what?

01:02:40.214 --> 01:02:42.175
I've had enough.

01:02:43.092 --> 01:02:44.510
Are you kicking me out again?

01:02:45.928 --> 01:02:46.763
I'm not leaving.

01:02:47.346 --> 01:02:48.973
Go ahead and try dragging me out.

01:02:52.018 --> 01:02:56.689
You've never stepped into the ring
and gotten your ass kicked.

01:02:56.773 --> 01:02:59.734
That's why you just sit there
trashing other people's films.

01:03:00.234 --> 01:03:04.655
He won't stop until he enters the ring
and gets beaten into a pulp.

01:03:06.032 --> 01:03:06.866
I don't care

01:03:08.075 --> 01:03:10.036
if it costs me billions of won.

01:03:11.329 --> 01:03:12.997
I'm going to teach this bastard a lesson.

01:03:16.959 --> 01:03:19.212
Hey, it's getting bad here. Go home.

01:03:19.295 --> 01:03:21.088
-Why? I don't want to.
-Just go.

01:03:21.172 --> 01:03:22.173
Hello, it's me.

01:03:23.800 --> 01:03:25.176
Instead of Ma Jae-yeong…

01:03:27.804 --> 01:03:30.348
we'll go with the runner-up's screenplay.

01:03:30.973 --> 01:03:33.226
Yes, Weather Maker by Hwang Dong-man.

01:03:38.022 --> 01:03:39.482
I'm going to let it fail.

01:03:40.608 --> 01:03:41.776
I'm going to let it fail completely,

01:03:42.401 --> 01:03:44.403
but I'll take comfort
in teaching someone a lesson.

01:03:44.487 --> 01:03:45.321
No way.

01:03:45.404 --> 01:03:47.615
No, I'm serious.
We're producing Hwang Dong-man's work.

01:03:48.825 --> 01:03:50.535
Yes, I'll see you tomorrow.

01:03:57.166 --> 01:03:58.000
You…

01:04:00.086 --> 01:04:01.295
are so dead.

01:04:02.880 --> 01:04:03.965
Step into the ring…

01:04:06.008 --> 01:04:07.260
and get your ass kicked.

01:04:11.430 --> 01:04:12.640
You can't run away.

01:04:26.445 --> 01:04:28.114
-Producer Kim!
-Yes?

01:04:28.197 --> 01:04:29.115
Put together a production team.

01:04:29.699 --> 01:04:30.533
Sorry?

01:04:49.218 --> 01:04:50.845
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

01:05:10.865 --> 01:05:12.241
This year's winner!

01:05:12.325 --> 01:05:14.410
We need to push Hwang Dong-man
to his limits.

01:05:14.493 --> 01:05:18.414
He can tremble in fear,
give up, and fall flat on his face.

01:05:18.497 --> 01:05:19.916
Who's Yeong-sil?

01:05:19.999 --> 01:05:21.083
It sounds like a pseudonym.

01:05:22.001 --> 01:05:24.921
Tell Yeong-sil I want to meet her.

01:05:25.630 --> 01:05:26.714
Did you borrow from a loan shark?

01:05:26.797 --> 01:05:29.467
Looks like this bastard
came into some money.

01:05:29.550 --> 01:05:31.594
He'll never complete a film at this rate.

01:05:31.677 --> 01:05:33.471
Good luck, Dong-man!

01:05:33.554 --> 01:05:35.765
Hwang Dong-man is really something.

01:05:36.349 --> 01:05:37.808
I'm so embarrassed by who I am right now

01:05:37.892 --> 01:05:40.061
that becoming
a slightly less embarrassing person

01:05:40.144 --> 01:05:41.395
is my purpose in life!

01:05:43.856 --> 01:05:48.861
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
